export const meta = {
  name: 'boot-of-doom-update-bundle',
  description: 'Gather everything needed to prepare a Boot of Doom repo UPDATE bundle for beamng.com',
  phases: [{ title: 'Gather', detail: 'template, current listing, changelog facts' }],
}

const REPO = 'C:\\Users\\ericr\\beamng-mcp'
const BOD = `${REPO}\\examples\\giant_props\\boot_of_doom`

const SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  additionalProperties: false,
  required: ['summary'],
  properties: {
    summary: { type: 'string' },
    facts: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        additionalProperties: false,
        required: ['claim', 'evidence'],
        properties: { claim: { type: 'string' }, evidence: { type: 'string' } },
      },
    },
    open_questions: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
  },
}

phase('Gather')

const results = await parallel([
  () =>
    agent(
      `Read every file in ${REPO}\\examples\\giant_props\\catapult_seesaw\\authoring\\repo_update\\ and
${REPO}\\examples\\giant_props\\catapult_seesaw\\dist\\repo_update\\.

That is this repo's ONLY worked example of a beamng.com resource UPDATE bundle (as opposed to a
first submission). I need to build the equivalent for Boot of Doom.

Report EXACTLY:
1. Every file in the bundle, its purpose, and its format (BBCode vs plain text vs markdown).
2. The exact structure/section order of UPLOAD.txt, quoted, so I can mirror it.
3. The exact structure of update_title.txt and update_description.bbcode - quote them in full.
4. How the certification block is formatted (I already update it programmatically).
5. Anything in the bundle that is generated by a script vs hand-written. Search the repo for any
   script that assembles dist/repo_update (compare with boot_of_doom/authoring/make_submission.py
   and football_goal_post's stage_upload.py if it exists).
6. Conventions the repo insists on for this content (search AGENTS.md and any listing/README docs
   for BBCode, XenForo, tagline length, version-numbering rules).

Do NOT modify any file.`,
      { label: 'gather:template', phase: 'Gather', schema: SCHEMA },
    ),
  () =>
    agent(
      `Read everything under ${BOD}\\authoring\\ (especially repo/, listing/, listing_copy.md,
make_submission.py, and the handoff json) plus ${BOD}\\dist\\repo_submission\\UPLOAD.txt and
description.bbcode.

Boot of Doom is ALREADY PUBLISHED on beamng.com (a YouTuber featured it). Its existing bundle is a
FIRST-SUBMISSION bundle ("Add resource", Version 1.0.0). I need to turn out an UPDATE bundle.

Report EXACTLY:
1. What the published listing says today - title, tagline, version, category, tags, description -
   quoting authoring/repo/*.txt and description.bbcode.
2. Which assets already exist and can be reused (icon, screenshots, thumbnails) and their paths.
3. What make_submission.py does step by step, and precisely which parts would need to change to
   emit an UPDATE bundle instead. Quote the relevant lines.
4. Any version string recorded anywhere in the repo for boot_of_doom (grep widely: fields.txt,
   UPLOAD.txt, CHANGELOG.md, spec.py, info.json, listing copy).
5. Whether info.json / info_standard.json inside the mod carry a version the game shows.

Do NOT modify any file.`,
      { label: 'gather:listing', phase: 'Gather', schema: SCHEMA },
    ),
  () =>
    agent(
      `I need an accurate, player-facing changelog for a Boot of Doom update.

The ONLY functional change since the published release is a fix to the shared Giant Props runtime
placement frame: runtime-created TSStatic parts (Boot of Doom's ten power-ladder segments and its
launch-angle needle) were positioned by dead reckoning from vehicle:getPosition()/getRotation().
getRotation() is stale after spawn, so on sloped terrain the console instruments detached from the
control panel - a metre off on a gentle slope, 11.5 m on a steep one. Now the frame is derived from
the vehicle's live node cloud.

VERIFY THIS IS THE WHOLE STORY, do not take my word for it:
1. Diff the CURRENT ${BOD}\\dist\\boot_of_doom_ericrolph.zip against the snapshot of the previously
   shipped release at
   C:\\Users\\ericr\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-ericr-beamng-mcp\\dd04b8ae-be00-400a-90fd-4e405f51dea3\\scratchpad\\zip_backup\\boot_of_doom__boot_of_doom_ericrolph.zip
   Report EXACTLY which members differ and how. If only runtime.lua differs, say so and diff it.
2. From that runtime.lua diff, list every behaviour change a PLAYER could notice - not just the
   instruments. Consider: does the change also move trigger volumes, particle effect directions, or
   the boot part itself on sloped ground? Read the diff carefully.
3. Check git log and CHANGELOG.md for anything else that landed for boot_of_doom since the
   published build.
4. Flag anything that is NOT player-visible so I do not put engineering detail in a player changelog.

Be precise and skeptical. Do NOT modify any file.`,
      { label: 'gather:changelog', phase: 'Gather', schema: SCHEMA },
    ),
])

return results.filter(Boolean)
